  "side": "Corp",
  "title": "Traps and net damage",
  "intro": "Not every face-down card in a remote is an agenda. Urtica Cipher is an asset that can be advanced like one; when the Runner accesses it, it does 2 net damage plus 1 per advancement token. Net damage discards cards from the Runner's grip at random — and a Runner who must discard more cards than they hold is flatlined and loses.\n\nYou installed Urtica Cipher and advanced it once. This lesson: advance it again, then let the Runner walk into it.",
  "outro": "Four cards gone from the Runner's grip for the price of two advancements. The Runner cannot tell a trap from an agenda from the outside, which is exactly why they will now hesitate over your next advanced card. That is the whole Corp track: money, servers, ice, scoring, and bluff. Press Enter to graduate to the starter game.",
